!____________________________________________________________________________________________________
!
! MASS-CORRECTED PRESTELLAR CORE CATALOGUE
! cloud: OrionA   distance: 432 pc   sources: 949
! Correction factor C_M = M_BE/M_reported on distance-invariant
! observables (SIGMA, CONC, RFOOT), decomposed into three
! multiplicative mass factors: C_M = F_FLUX * F_BG * F_TEMP
! (flux recovery x background subtraction x temperature bias).
! INIT = reported SED fit; CORR = M_INIT * C_M (true mass).
!
!____________________________________________________________________________________________________
!
! TABULATED QUANTITIES:
!
!  1 NO                    Source running number (from getsf)
!  2 WCS_ACOOR    deg      WCS (J2000) alpha-coordinate
!  3 WCS_DCOOR    deg      WCS (J2000) delta-coordinate
!  4 SIGMA        cm^-2    Background column PEAK^BGF on the 13.5" H2 band
!  5 CONC                  Peak-to-mean concentration PEAK^SRC/(FXT/area)
!  6 RFOOT                 Footprint-to-size ratio sqrt(FOOA*FOOB)/sqrt(AFWHM*BFWHM)
!  7 T_INIT       K        Initial (reported) SED dust temperature
!  8 T_INIT_ERR   K        Uncertainty of T_INIT
!  9 M_INIT       Msun     Initial (reported) SED mass
! 10 M_INIT_ERR   Msun     Total uncertainty of M_INIT (fit + opacity + dust/gas)
! 11 CHI2                  chi^2 of the initial SED fit
! 12 DOF                   Degrees of freedom (N_bands - 2)
! 13 QUALITY               Fit quality: ok if CHI2 < DOF+1, else bad
! 14 F_FLUX                Flux-recovery mass factor (footprint flux loss)
! 15 F_BG                  Background-subtraction mass factor FXSDbsl/FXSDbs (interp->true crater)
! 16 F_TEMP                Temperature-bias mass factor (residual; internal T gradient)
! 17 C_M                   Total correction factor = F_FLUX * F_BG * F_TEMP = M_BE/M_reported
! 18 M_CORR       Msun     Corrected true mass = M_INIT * C_M
! 19 M_CORR_ERR   Msun     Uncertainty of M_CORR
! 20 C_M_4D                Four-observable correction factor (+physical size; needs DISTANCE); paper-adopted
! 21 M_CORR_4D    Msun     Corrected mass from C_M_4D = M_INIT * C_M_4D
! 22 T_RECOV      K        Recovery-corrected SED temperature (flux-boosted refit)
! 23 T_RECOV_ERR  K        Uncertainty of T_RECOV
! 24 M_RECOV      Msun     Recovery-corrected SED mass (flux-boosted refit; = M_INIT*F_FLUX)
! 25 M_RECOV_ERR  Msun     Uncertainty of M_RECOV
! 26 C_MMASS               Mass-indexed factor (distance-dependent; diagnostic only)
! 27 FOOT_AS      arcsec   Footprint radius sqrt(FOOA*FOOB)/2, the fourth observable
! 28 EXTRAP_3D             1 if the three-observable prediction was bounded to its neighbours range, i.e. extrapolated
! 29 EXTRAP_4D             1 if the four-observable prediction was extrapolated, or no fourth observable existed
! 30 SUPPORT_3D            Standardised distance to the furthest training sample used by the three-observable fit
! 31 SUPPORT_4D            Standardised distance to the furthest training sample used by the four-observable fit
! 32 IN_HULL_3D            1 if the three observables lie inside the convex hull of the training set
! 33 IN_HULL_4D            1 if the four observables lie inside the convex hull of the training set
! 34 IN_DOMAIN             1 if both hull tests pass; the recommended reliability filter
!____________________________________________________________________________________________________
!
! NOTES ON nan VALUES:
!   T_RECOV, M_RECOV (+ errors): the recovery-corrected refit boosts each
!     SED band by its model flux-recovery fraction and refits; it needs at
!     least two bands with a valid recovery fraction.  A few sources sit
!     outside the per-band recovery-interpolation hull (mainly at 160 um,
!     which can be in absorption) in more than one band and cannot be
!     refit -> nan.  M_CORR (= M_INIT * C_M) is unaffected and always finite.
!   C_MMASS: distance-dependent, mass-indexed diagnostic from a 4-D
!     interpolation (mass + the three observables); its hull is smaller
!     than the 3-D C_M corrector, so sources just outside it are nan.
!     It is diagnostic only and not used in the correction.
!   All other columns (SIGMA..M_CORR_ERR) are finite for every listed
!     source: only QUALITY==ok sources inside the C_M hull are written,
!     and fit errors are defined down to 2-band (DOF=0) fits.
!
!____________________________________________________________________________________________________
!
!      NO     WCS_ACOOR     WCS_DCOOR       SIGMA     CONC    RFOOT   T_INIT T_INIT_ERR       M_INIT   M_INIT_ERR      CHI2  DOF  QUALITY   F_FLUX     F_BG   F_TEMP      C_M       M_CORR   M_CORR_ERR   C_M_4D    M_CORR_4D  T_RECOV T_RECOV_ERR      M_RECOV  M_RECOV_ERR  C_MMASS   FOOT_AS  EXTRAP_3D  EXTRAP_4D  SUPPORT_3D  SUPPORT_4D  IN_HULL_3D  IN_HULL_4D  IN_DOMAIN
        1    84.8324805    -7.4364542  3.0740e+22    6.171    3.617   19.600      1.400  8.49534e+00  2.88534e+00     0.484    2       ok    1.059    1.633    0.994    1.718  1.45983e+01  4.95813e+00    1.133  9.62617e+00   19.600       2.250  8.95930e+00  3.57934e+00      nan     24.45          0          0      0.7772      0.9866           1           1          1
        1    84.0787115    -6.3701824  4.6810e+22    4.035    2.434   20.600      1.700  7.95283e+00  2.82679e+00     0.534    2       ok    0.979    1.635    0.805    1.289  1.02538e+01  3.64464e+00    1.109  8.81794e+00   21.900       3.400  7.83186e+00  3.52427e+00      nan     21.43          0          0      0.3626      0.5609           1           1          1
